      *
      *The compiler-directing statements and the conditional compilation
      *directives, which are an IBM extension. A conditional directive
      *must be specified entirely on one line, and AS, DEFINED, PARAMETER,
      *OVERRIDE and OFF belong to directive syntax alone.
      *
      *Member: CBLDIR   Compilable: no (directives and declarations only)
      *Source: ILE COBOL Language Reference SC09-2539, compiler
      *        directives and compiler-directing statements.
      *Retrieved: 2026-07-29
      *
      *The PROCESS statement names compiler options ahead of the
      *Identification Division, overriding the CRTCBLMOD and
      *CRTBNDCBL parameters. Only the first line carries the word
      *PROCESS; the options continue over further lines and end at
      *the separator period. Conflicting options are legal, and the
      *last one encountered takes precedence, which is what lets
      *this statement carry the whole of Appendix G's tables.
       PROCESS
           APOST BASICOPT BLK CHGPOSSGN CRTARKIDX CRTF CVTPICGGRAPHIC
           CVTPICNGRAPHIC CVTPICXGRAPHIC CVTTODATE DATE DATETIME
           DDSFILLER DUPKEYCHK FLOAT FULLOPT GEN HIGH INTERMEDIATE
           INZDLT LINENUMBER LINKPGM LINKPRC MAP MINIMUM MONOPIC
           MONOPRC NEVEROPTIMIZE NOBLK NOCHGPOSSGN NOCRTARKIDX NOCRTF
           NOCVTPICGGRAPHIC NOCVTPICNGRAPHIC NOCVTPICXGRAPHIC
           NOCVTTODATE NODATE NODATETIME NODDSFILLER NODUPKEYCHK
           NOFIPS NOFLOAT NOGEN NOINZDLT NOMAP NOMONOPIC NOMONOPRC
           NONUMBER NOOBSOLETE NOOPTIMIZE NOOPTIONS NOOUTPUT
           NOPRTCORR NORANGE NOSECLVL NOSEQUENCE NOSOURCE NOSRC
           NOSTDINZ NOSTDTRUNC NOSYNC NOTIME NOTIMESTAMP NOUNREF
           NOVARCHAR NOVBSUM NOXREF NUMBER OBSOLETE OPTIONS OUTPUT
           PRTCORR QUOTE RANGE SECLVL SEQUENCE SOURCE SRC STDINZ
           STDINZHEX00 STDTRUNC SYNC TIME TIMESTAMP UNREF VARCHAR
           VBSUM XREF
           GENLVL(20) FLAG(10) NOPGMINFO NOCOMPRESSDBG COMPRESSDBG
           EXTDSPOPT(DFRWRT UNDSPCHR ACCUPDALL)
           EXTDSPOPT(NODFRWRT NOUNDSPCHR ACCUPDNE)
           SRTSEQ(HEX) SRTSEQ(JOB) SRTSEQ(JOBRUN) SRTSEQ(LANGIDUNQ)
           SRTSEQ(LANGIDSHR) LANGID(JOB) LANGID(JOBRUN)
           ENBPFRCOL(PEP) ENBPFRCOL(ENTRYEXIT) ENBPFRCOL(FULL)
           PRFDTA(COL) PRFDTA(NOCOL) CCSID(JOB) CCSID(JOBRUN) CCSID(HEX)
           NTLCCSID(13488) NTLPADCHAR(NX"0020")
           DATTIM(1900 40) ARITHMETIC(NOEXTEND) ARITHMETIC(EXTEND31)
           ARITHMETIC(EXTEND31FULL) ARITHMETIC(EXTEND63)
           THREAD(NOTHREAD) THREAD(SERIALIZE)
           OPTVALUE(NOOPT) OPTVALUE(OPT) LICOPT("NoSTRICT")
           PGMINFO(PCML MODULE)
           STGMDL(INHERIT) STGMDL(SNGLVL) STGMDL(TERASPACE)
           ACTGRP(STGMDL) ACTGRP(NEW) ACTGRP(CALLER).
      *
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. CBLDIR.
      *
      *Listing control, an IBM extension: *CONTROL or *CBL turns the
      *source listing off and on, EJECT starts a new page, SKIP
      *spaces it, and TITLE names it.
           *CONTROL NOSOURCE
           *CBL SOURCE
           EJECT
           SKIP1
           SKIP2
           SKIP3
           TITLE "Order register listing"
      *
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
      *COPY brings in a member, and REPLACE rewrites text from here
      *on. Both are Standard COBOL and reserved words.
           COPY ORDWS.
           REPLACE ==WS-== BY ==ORD-==.
           REPLACE OFF.
      *
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN-PARA.
      *Defining compilation variables: a literal with and without AS,
      *a hex and a Boolean literal, an arithmetic expression, a
      *variable taken from the CRTBNDCBL DEFINE parameter, one
      *redefined, and one removed.
           >>DEFINE DEBUG AS B"1"
           >>DEFINE REL-LEVEL 12
           >>DEFINE EYE-CATCHER AS X"F1F2"
           >>DEFINE MAXIMUM AS 40 + 2
           >>DEFINE FROM-COMMAND AS PARAMETER
           >>DEFINE REL-LEVEL AS 13 OVERRIDE
           >>DEFINE DEBUG OFF
      *
      *One-way and two-way selection. DEFINED tests whether a
      *variable exists, and the predefined variables the compiler
      *supplies, ARCH and COMPILER-VRM among them, are tested the
      *same way.
           >>IF DEBUG IS DEFINED
               DISPLAY "debug build" UPON SYSOUT
           >>ELSE
               CONTINUE
           >>END-IF
           >>IF ARCH >= 10
               CONTINUE
           >>END-IF
           >>IF FROM-COMMAND IS NOT DEFINED
               DISPLAY "no override" UPON SYSOUT
           >>END-IF
      *
      *Multi-branch selection, with THROUGH ranges and OTHER.
           >>EVALUATE REL-LEVEL
           >>WHEN 12
               DISPLAY "twelve" UPON SYSOUT
           >>WHEN 13 THROUGH 15
               DISPLAY "newer" UPON SYSOUT
           >>WHEN OTHER
               DISPLAY "unknown" UPON SYSOUT
           >>END-EVALUATE
           >>EVALUATE TRUE
           >>WHEN COMPILER-VRM >= 7050000
               CONTINUE
           >>WHEN OTHER
               CONTINUE
           >>END-EVALUATE
           GOBACK.
